  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 206 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nLittle change in the upper level pattern as westerlies aloft prevail \nthrough at least mid-week before a trough develops over the Western \nCONUS leading to weak ridging into Iowa. Expect wildfire smoke to \npersist over Iowa until the trough develops to the west and changes \nthe source region of the upper flow. This smoke remains dense\nenough for solar filtering and perhaps will result in slightly\ncooler temperatures than forecast. The little change in the \npattern will also keep the surface boundary in the vicinity of \nIowa through Wednesday then it will shift a bit south into \nMissouri. On and off chances for thunderstorms will occur during\nthis period, especially during the overnight hours as the LLJ \nfuels thunderstorm development in addition to the periodic short\nwave passages. Thunderstorm chances will continue to end the \nweek despite the arrival of cooler air as an overrunning event \nof the surface boundary appears possible. Heat index values may\neclipse 100 degrees Tuesday and Wednesday over central and\nsouthern Iowa but at this time, should remain below headline\ncriteria.",
